# Testing Conventions

EventBook uses two test layers. Match the layer to the file you are editing.

## Vitest (unit/integration)

- Colocate tests as `src/**/*.test.ts` next to the source file under test.
- Reference shape: @src/lib/utils.test.ts
- Config: @vitest.config.ts
- Run all unit tests: `npm test`
- Run one file: `npx vitest run src/lib/utils.test.ts`

When adding a new `src/pages/api/**` endpoint, add at least one Vitest test covering the handler logic or extracted pure functions.

## Playwright (E2E)

- Place specs in `tests/**/*.spec.ts` — not under `src/`.
- Config: @playwright.config.ts
- Run E2E: `npx playwright test`
- Auth flows (`/auth/signin`, `/auth/signup`, `/dashboard` guard) require E2E coverage before merge.

Use `page.goto('/')` against the local dev server; do not hardcode external URLs in new specs.

## General

- Prefer testing behavior and return values, not implementation details.
- Do not skip tests without a tracked reason in the test name or a linked issue.
- CI currently runs lint + build only (@.github/workflows/ci.yml); still run `npm test` locally before PRs.

See @AGENTS.md for repo-wide rules and @context/foundation/prd.md for MVP scope.
